Subject: [PATCH] P-009: make validate cheaper than a full parse

After P-008, validate cost 1.27-1.81x the instructions of a full parse.
Numbers ran a token-length prescan and read_num on a stack copy, strings
used a byte-at-a-time scanner, and whitespace was skipped one byte at a
time.

Read a number in place when it starts before the last byte outside
[0-9A-Za-z+.-]: read_num only reads past a byte in that set, so that
byte stops it inside the buffer. Certify strict-grammar numbers below
1e308 without the float conversion and send everything else to
read_num. Near eof, copy only the token and the byte after it. Under
NUMBER_AS_RAW or BIGNUM_AS_RAW every number takes the copy path, so
the NUL stored through pre never lands in the caller buffer.

Inline read_str_validate with read_str's 16-byte ASCII unroll, an
8-byte word test, and the 4-byte UTF-8 loops, each only while enough
bytes remain. Skip indentation two spaces at a time. Replace the
container element count with first-value states after an opening
bracket, and give out-of-line readers a copy of cur.

Results, messages, positions and nesting depth still match the full
reader for the six flags fastjson uses.

